#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096460 :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=-2 \\\\ x+y+2z &=-1 \\\\ x+2y+z &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n\n\n$$\nM= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=-2 \\\\ y &=3 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757033 :question-generator/id #uuid "98dda97a-0c34-5d23-8a2e-9660f5991a11" :question-generator/script "generators/7a/7abf2c7dfdd446626f3a453874c25e6568f7196510aed61eaf19bbb3e7b019d2/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38b8de74-9b19-5fcb-86d1-d4eb77627541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638} {:answer/id #uuid "82fe070f-9ba8-572e-807f-b7e3a637c60e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$, $y=2$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340305} {:answer/id #uuid "98a029ca-6087-5b72-9ca2-e3147cdb70a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=-5$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340507} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e3c2ea-d16f-581b-9b65-22d05f5e48ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=5$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341062} {:answer/id #uuid "e383876d-902d-5a68-82a6-fe6aedf0fd52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1$, $y=-6$, and $z=-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38b8de74-9b19-5fcb-86d1-d4eb77627541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339638} :answer-field/id #uuid "18caed8a-a8c5-5f22-b7e0-3310a888fea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-73396" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=8 \\\\ -2x+2y-3z &=-11 \\\\ x+z &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=8 \\\\ y-z &=1 \\\\ z &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5) &=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5) &=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "affc0ad4-801a-5399-8a47-b7526facc7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403628} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb21bbb-79ee-5df3-9904-5df560da18c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403629} {:answer/id #uuid "c5805566-431b-59b1-b5d4-027282fdf8a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403630} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4c1b86-80d7-59f5-af00-319d8bf12b68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403631} {:answer/id #uuid "76bc4cc9-6acc-5be4-bff8-66f385a06fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4c1b86-80d7-59f5-af00-319d8bf12b68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403631} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15e152b-e602-5625-9a15-cb468ccf6dd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403627}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e85abf79-3b58-57ed-b3d6-9f31cc3b2817" :question/math-academy-id "q-73397" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543df558-b8a5-545b-b160-2fe37379c9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} {:answer/id #uuid "c42f8e88-729f-5ad1-b070-bff1132c48a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264714} {:answer/id #uuid "c483a5fe-745e-59db-8de7-5c8a3454d240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264721} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a50c5-13c6-5393-8129-945ea4016aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} :answer-field/id #uuid "091832d1-1a63-50c1-8342-a7864cc522dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265260}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f61c846d-507f-5371-aeef-030ef902e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130928" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{7}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d3cb3a6-9b25-5f14-b7fe-ef0f81082c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339832} {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} {:answer/id #uuid "82ffd466-0e67-5425-9c00-af468a2c3588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340306} {:answer/id #uuid "af2f918c-cf0f-5b21-8e87-4c608c0f9852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340724} {:answer/id #uuid "c76cf58e-617a-5441-8169-40443447226f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6637df9f-50f4-58dd-8cf1-2dded102c657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf34cc2-5873-5eaf-970b-9dc56a73754a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4fabb78b-3a40-50c6-9149-8d79603a31f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73579" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+6y-3z &=18 \\\\ -4x+8y-3z &=2 \\\\ y-4z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-6 \\\\ y-4z &=-3 \\\\ z &=-22,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22) &=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22) &=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c85a87-f9d3-5992-bd65-769c46e1d92d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339203} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} {:answer/id #uuid "266e54c3-4543-5283-9017-83d16e10e193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339463} {:answer/id #uuid "32af4883-fe55-53ee-8722-a0f084a72e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339575} {:answer/id #uuid "79208760-a400-5994-ac65-f0b5469feeb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fbe2b87-90d4-5154-8a7b-4cbe5d76ee8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339272} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0944fb0-08b1-53ae-b7d8-bc6730da208f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341713}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3624bdf6-d1bf-5873-8a2a-1542d72f9250" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z &=3 \\\\ y+5z &=-8 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4) &=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4) &=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f84b955-e25e-5955-8a2a-87d8b550463b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨52,21,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339543} {:answer/id #uuid "304cea0c-89a4-55c8-b0d0-dffbc12bb18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339549} {:answer/id #uuid "35874527-0d05-510c-938e-52c64b49f406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339602} {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} {:answer/id #uuid "e70f0c3f-b109-5746-a6d9-5b910dad1d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57014e05-78ee-56aa-a36c-1a4147653d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f662ab-5ce0-5cde-8194-11854041cc57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341727}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a6417a9-7e20-54a9-9651-61368745cde5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73588" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=-2 \\\\ y+2z &=-1 \\\\ z &=11,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=11$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(11) &=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-23$ and $z=11$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-23)+3(11) &=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-58$, $y=-23$, and $z=11.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-58,-23,11⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} {:answer/id #uuid "3493c0b1-471a-5165-b338-34b981a66bfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339595} {:answer/id #uuid "3670b23e-82b8-5a09-8d82-457c528c5b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339614} {:answer/id #uuid "b35d9857-7680-5d0d-9437-cc48d8d3277a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340757} {:answer/id #uuid "bd407622-a505-57f5-ad35-f323345504ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061b84d7-0a88-5827-a09a-0ae94645e28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339179} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa4b0ec2-bc66-5a30-b57d-09c5803067da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341676}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ecd0e17-9926-5c80-9527-2ab263ac9de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73592" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y+3z &=-6 \\\\ 2x-4y+3z &=-1 \\\\ 2y-4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9341f62-c8f8-570d-80c8-63278f533fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368711} {:answer/id #uuid "cf00639b-8c94-5353-94da-3f2b856bf365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368712} {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} {:answer/id #uuid "3baa2212-ba77-51f2-be2f-5e043a5564f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=10$, $y=3$, and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368714} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d5251-f525-5757-9a3a-816f522e1513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=16$, $y=5$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8d2c28-de03-52ea-8fb5-2bfbbb958a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f809106-1e50-5a91-813a-0a376c6d5c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-73587" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=1 \\\\ y-z &=-4 \\\\ z &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(1) &=-4\\,⟹\\,y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3(-3) &=1\\,⟹\\,x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e0739b-acd3-5213-baab-e978002551c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400515} {:answer/id #uuid "09aec1aa-dcc4-5694-820b-48b65b045141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400516} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea67907-7f4c-52b6-b879-e7a1aaa740f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400517} {:answer/id #uuid "06e6ab1e-4b01-5e52-ba1d-2553cc1a9411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400518} {:answer/id #uuid "fc215d6c-0ef8-5f56-9172-bb0f8dae360e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09aec1aa-dcc4-5694-820b-48b65b045141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400516} :answer-field/id #uuid "924e4677-652c-5aa5-ad82-4e9a728fb938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400514}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" :question/math-academy-id "q-130927" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=4 \\\\ -3x-6y+4z &=-8 \\\\ 3x+7y-z &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=4 \\\\ y+2z &=-2 \\\\ z &=4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4) &=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4) &=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbb2c9b-2424-5248-830c-2c1f0a65a08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403656} {:answer/id #uuid "090537bb-6f40-5836-9945-a970355e758b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403657} {:answer/id #uuid "fab64420-cace-555b-aa98-7c62e22daa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403658} {:answer/id #uuid "bb59ea2b-37e2-5ba0-85a8-5281bf3bc593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403659} {:answer/id #uuid "24b18c66-2b96-5dd6-a905-03f61b72ec8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb59ea2b-37e2-5ba0-85a8-5281bf3bc593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403659} :answer-field/id #uuid "45e63128-e41c-54ad-afda-6808e4f902e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403655}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09ed8746-0452-52a7-a619-929b2d587f13" :question/math-academy-id "q-73580" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414019} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414022} {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} {:answer/id #uuid "8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414025} {:answer/id #uuid "979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414030}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73593" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+6y-3z &=-1 \\\\ -2x-12y+8z &=1 \\\\ -x-5y+4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bebd905-0240-52d0-968d-938c33de08ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-18,8,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639474} {:answer/id #uuid "0fcc8ddf-a247-5188-81f5-991e48007571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639483} {:answer/id #uuid "315919a9-e034-5a79-858b-4903e68687b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-24,10,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639542} {:answer/id #uuid "e0af81a2-e277-564c-87e2-cbf9fa1b30ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨26,-8,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639804} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e5c542-626e-5e72-9e3a-2d14fb66fe15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨16,-5,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "315919a9-e034-5a79-858b-4903e68687b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-24,10,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639542} :answer-field/id #uuid "da5c3e10-a3dc-5dae-b3e7-e412d2853970" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dc08be3-c769-502f-bf78-0a4feb848af1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73577" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-4z &=4 \\\\ x+2y-z &=-1 \\\\ y+3z &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z &=2 \\\\ y+3z &=1 \\\\ z &=-3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-3$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+3(-3) &=1\\,⟹\\,y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=10$ and $z=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(10)-2(-3) &=2\\,⟹\\,x=-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-24$, $y=10$, and $z=-3.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-24,10,-3⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186756998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adceadb7-5698-5ba3-902e-3bc7bf839851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757016} {:answer/id #uuid "b96201b0-44c1-5e5e-b110-e196c1c857ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757019} {:answer/id #uuid "bb949d01-f847-5ae2-a5c9-c568c6e81646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757020} {:answer/id #uuid "bd52b8f1-4ca5-5518-ab79-c36e482b621a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757022} {:answer/id #uuid "cb015c85-9906-5b23-bc3c-38b140fe3654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96201b0-44c1-5e5e-b110-e196c1c857ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757019} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd22473-befe-55a6-be59-70afec1d15ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "060af8c1-e26e-579e-83e1-d0f6c0b2b802" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-9y &=0 \\\\ 2x+6y-z &=3 \\\\ -2x-7y+z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=-1R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-1R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d47904-1296-51da-99b5-2d7d8575f749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-9,-1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757005} {:answer/id #uuid "68ec9139-afcc-51b3-be24-48c4d0a19616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,2,-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757010} {:answer/id #uuid "75a05541-0e8a-508b-83dc-752a1abe700d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-17,-5,-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757012} {:answer/id #uuid "b547149b-af32-578e-a9da-412f7702ead7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(7,3,-1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757017} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eebee3-ed29-5809-9209-75aca5191cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-18,-4,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7eebee3-ed29-5809-9209-75aca5191cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-18,-4,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757018} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6b99498-3513-5396-b1c9-949fc609cc72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63a85e4a-d05b-5eca-9202-d889f4d8cbfb" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+3y+2z &=0 \\\\ x-3y-3z &=3 \\\\ -2x+8y+2z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-1R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-1R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-3 \\\\ y &=-1-(-1)(-3) \\\\ &=-4 \\\\ x &=0-(-3)(-4) \\\\ &\\quad -(-2)(-3) \\\\ &=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(-18,-4,-3\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a92d1d9-fdda-5f46-853c-c8b923efd984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(9,11,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757000} {:answer/id #uuid "101b969b-d8da-52ab-a407-81ff7e527c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-25,-6,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757001} {:answer/id #uuid "10364258-1db9-5415-abc9-6d0450049b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-13,-2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757002} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cb3cbf-d0b3-54ba-8781-cc85989a6162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-7,3,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757025} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe56609-eae4-5504-a3c9-85797c67870f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(5,7,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0cb3cbf-d0b3-54ba-8781-cc85989a6162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-7,3,-4\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757025} :answer-field/id #uuid "6be22918-8ee0-5a73-afb2-9024d55d9c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757011}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87c67b19-2b31-5c31-a830-94bab02c0bf2" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=\\frac{1}{3}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-4 \\\\ y &=3-(0)(-4) \\\\ &=3 \\\\ x &=-5-(-2)(3) \\\\ &\\quad -(-2)(-4) \\\\ &=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(-7,3,-4\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a5b4d5-96d1-59db-98b3-7055a705a173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-19,-7,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186756999} {:answer/id #uuid "1783fe2f-7350-5ac6-8a27-09a181249294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(19,5,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757003} {:answer/id #uuid "bdca9560-7b65-5003-a5b1-a32fc045a0f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(8,2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757023} {:answer/id #uuid "cdaab2c7-b756-502b-8030-f13732b39ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-2,-2,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757027} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f172c4-e666-55ff-8830-72a7d1816a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-5,-3,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1783fe2f-7350-5ac6-8a27-09a181249294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(19,5,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757003} :answer-field/id #uuid "36100d49-b552-5d7b-9be2-ba1fc3ffd73f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dc5d6c8-0139-5220-8d45-fe4bded0ce05" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y+3z &=-12 \\\\ 2x-6y-4z &=8 \\\\ -2x+4y-2z &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 9 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -18\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -18\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -18\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & -10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=0 \\\\ y &=5-(2)(0) \\\\ &=5 \\\\ x &=4-(-3)(5) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(0) \\\\ &=19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(19,5,0\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ff0381-67d3-5998-91a0-45a3dc47d372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757007} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5cb553-8022-5fc5-ba89-35bfbc9a047f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757015} {:answer/id #uuid "be84635e-2b68-5138-9d17-5e5c90fee3a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757024} {:answer/id #uuid "df8a3a8c-3067-5b41-95ac-40631027eacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757030} {:answer/id #uuid "f75fcf2d-06d5-5b73-a43b-36567f429da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be84635e-2b68-5138-9d17-5e5c90fee3a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757024} :answer-field/id #uuid "272d888d-babf-527e-8bc4-c16889c578ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd4bec18-420e-5a7e-8c05-e86723f9ab68" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -4 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize the first pivot with $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nNormalize with $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c5babc5-f223-5d99-84f1-f4807792f441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757046} {:answer/id #uuid "54892b6a-9372-5cdc-8728-12e0bec7a0ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757047} {:answer/id #uuid "950ad8a3-a6d6-5f53-b29b-81823a881765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757055} {:answer/id #uuid "95671fe6-b2f1-512d-b5c8-38b2ceff74fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757056} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb84122-f6f7-5e29-9722-43d66cbe3890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c5babc5-f223-5d99-84f1-f4807792f441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757046} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff140869-99be-5530-a54f-fac57d81520e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757068}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d6b8129-3696-5a59-89b3-efcd248b7a09" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=-2 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=1 \\\\ y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757044 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "089ad372-a6b6-5012-bd8e-5c495f4c959e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-4,-3,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757035} {:answer/id #uuid "249a25e5-ceda-5203-864b-6eaa4d067123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,1,0\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757041} {:answer/id #uuid "48968c25-d43d-5f47-91b8-9267e029e085" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-6,-5,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757045} {:answer/id #uuid "93a9d4e5-b102-5a05-a5cc-47bb0c3166b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2,-1,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757054} {:answer/id #uuid "acec38ec-694b-519c-b34a-94534ef14fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,0,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93a9d4e5-b102-5a05-a5cc-47bb0c3166b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2,-1,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757054} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce713a4-3738-58c2-a5eb-e1cb65fe41b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757048}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43d434df-4fe0-572f-8092-df01f458b6f0" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-z &=2 \\\\ -x+2y+2z &=0 \\\\ -x+3y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=2 \\\\ y &=1-(1)(2) \\\\ &=-1 \\\\ x &=2-(-2)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(2) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(2,-1,2\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035ff279-287b-5828-b15c-1d53b40ed674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(3,1,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757034} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba9a4f4-3c9d-5b75-8192-c332c987359f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(5,2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757050} {:answer/id #uuid "702898dc-5152-5d90-94f5-60a19634fe7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,0,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757051} {:answer/id #uuid "8137113d-8174-59e4-93da-b3c06683c8af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-4,-5,3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757053} {:answer/id #uuid "d21007a3-ac69-5467-b531-244c4d19d5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(0,-3,3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "702898dc-5152-5d90-94f5-60a19634fe7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,0,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757051} :answer-field/id #uuid "097cf6cf-7ab0-500b-8e9c-53820a0e7fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757036}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6575f85d-7aac-53f1-b121-353f331e6bc9" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-z &=3 \\\\ x-2y &=1 \\\\ x-y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-2 \\\\ y &=-2-(1)(-2) \\\\ &=0 \\\\ x &=3-(-2)(0) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(-2) \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(1,0,-2\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10250073-5db8-5db8-9c61-1b21f1c54a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,-1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757038} {:answer/id #uuid "1538c7c1-bb2e-58b1-a917-9abe40e0d6c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,-1,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757039} {:answer/id #uuid "3d2fcba7-0ed6-573b-a7b8-e9b4e94f3d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2,0,2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757043} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4c2928-d48d-5b6d-a5e9-9d887d060158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-2,-4,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757057} {:answer/id #uuid "f95152d0-f704-551b-aa50-33665d332b7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-1,-3,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10250073-5db8-5db8-9c61-1b21f1c54a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1,-1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757038} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce659242-8034-5ea4-8706-058cb83ef478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5bdf71e-ebab-5543-be28-3273bcd44d39" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-3 \\\\ y &=-1-(0)(-3) \\\\ &=-1 \\\\ x &=2-(-1)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad -(0)(-3) \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(1,-1,-3\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "161cd6fb-ac5e-5a01-91a0-06b484f89777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-1,1,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757040} {:answer/id #uuid "26a90c42-55a7-59bb-ad2a-afe53c2bd562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-1,2,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757042} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd69249-d4e3-5078-bbb4-c73f3bd521f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-5,5,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757052} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fae520-1c87-594a-b53b-202e6d359909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,-3,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757059} {:answer/id #uuid "db7ee354-f98e-54ae-b1be-4b825ca4b056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-3,3,-3\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8fae520-1c87-594a-b53b-202e6d359909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4,-3,-2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757059} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7e3223-cf2d-57a0-81c7-2a28c58e1717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757060}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec343d89-4a32-5dd8-9fa7-33e20598d3b0" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=3 \\\\ -x-y+2z &=-5 \\\\ y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=-2 \\\\ y &=-3-(0)(-2) \\\\ &=-3 \\\\ x &=3-(1)(-3) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(-2) \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(4,-3,-2\\right)\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a0edf1-af6b-5428-aec1-b7b5ed58ef26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757081} {:answer/id #uuid "6a00caa2-399c-52a8-b0fd-a0f6bcad7566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757084} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4e0828-da20-58d4-be26-e8f7c5ee3b0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757086} {:answer/id #uuid "c74a2