 augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186757085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dcd6404-1c55-5e68-91c7-88fc60ae88cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757088} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d52fce-ad41-5dbb-a81b-3bcc6e5174f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757091} {:answer/id #uuid "af71baf4-2e72-5252-b557-3a79d2e8a981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186757093} {:answer/id #uuid "da32653a-e8